! jb_ax5b "I-Box 5", routine 1262 ("TEST EX AND EXIC"), TEST 2B --
! "CHK EXIC OF NON BRANCH CLASS INSTRUCTIONS".  THE TWO ENDS OF TEST 2B
! AROUND THE MIDDLE THAT IS ALREADY TRANSCRIBED.
!
!   023742.40-023767.40 (PDF p.101) is programs/ax5b_162_exic_classes.strap
!                                   / verify_ax5b_162_exic_listing.py.
!   THIS FILE is the two ends around it:
!       HEAD  023705.00-023742.00, PDF p.99 whole + the 5 rows that spill
!             onto PDF p.100.  59 half-words.
!       TAIL  023770.00-024000.00, PDF p.102.  17 half-words.
!   76 rows here + 43 rows there = 119, and 023705.00 through 024000.00
!   inclusive is 119 half-words.  TEST 2B and routine 1262's TEST 2B exit
!   are now transcribed end to end with nothing left behind.
!
!   THE TWO FILES DO NOT OVERLAP, checked on the ASSEMBLED IMAGE and not
!   on the row lists: the second SLC moves the location counter and
!   deposits nothing.  Assembling this program writes 39 words; of the
!   words between the segments only 023742 exists, because this file's
!   last head row 023742.00 "BD,I6266" is that word's LEFT half.  Its
!   right half 023742.40 -- the sibling's first row -- assembles here as
!   00000000, and words 023743-023767 are absent from the image.
!
! CITED BY PDF PAGE.  jb_ax5b's LISTING pages carry no printed page
! numbers -- the "12 11 10 9" down the left margin is fanfold
! carriage-tape line numbering, and the only printed numbers are in the
! front write-up, which is scanned 2-up.  Every verify_ax5b_*.py here
! already says "PDF p.NN" for that reason.
!
! ------------------------------------------------------------------
! WHAT TEST 2B IS, ESTABLISHED FROM THESE PAGES AND NOT FROM A BLOCK MAP
! ------------------------------------------------------------------
! Entry label I6260 at 023705.00, PDF p.99, first printed row of the
! block; last row 024000.00 on PDF p.102.  Its own header comment:
!
!   023705.00  I6260 LVI,$X1,I62INT  "-TEST 2B, CHK EXIC OF NON BRANCH"
!   023705.40        SV,$X1,$IA      "-CLASS INSTRUCTIONS, DIR IX."
!
! FIVE classes, in this printed order, each announced by a one-word
! comment on the first row of its setup and each identified beyond doubt
! by the "LX,$X1,<subject>" row that loads the subject instruction:
!
!   class        setup at    subject     subject's content (PDF p.109,
!                                        verify_ax5b_162_int_entry_listing)
!   DIR IX       023705.00   I62EX  024322.00  LX,$X1,I00O
!   IMMED IX     023722.40   I62EXI 024332.00  LVI,$X1,%8@777777.40
!   MISC         023735.00   I62EXM 024331.00  Z,$X1
!   FLT PT       023747.00   I62EXF 024330.00  L(U),I00O
!   FULL WD VFL  023762.00   I62EXV 024327.00  L(BU),I00O   <- FULL LENGTH
!
! THREE RULES PER CLASS, each with its own error entry.  This is the
! point of the block and it is literal, not inferred:
!
!   (a) EXIC to that class must NOT interrupt.
!       The setup plants the class's own error label into the interrupt
!       table entry I62ITE ("LVI,$X1,I626n / SVA,$X1,I62ITE"), zeroes
!       $IND and $MASK, and issues "EXIC,I62PSI".  If an interruption
!       happens, control lands on I626n = "SIC,SEN / B,SERS" with
!       "-INT WHEN EXIC TO / -A <class> INSTR."  If it does not, the
!       straight-line "BD,I626n+1" skips past the error entry.
!   (b) The subject instruction must have EXECUTED.
!       "LX,$X1,<reg>" reloads the register the subject was supposed to
!       change, then "SIC,SEN / B{Z}XVZ,SERS" with
!       "-SUBJ INST WAS <class> / -AND WAS NOT EXECUTED."
!   (c) The PSEUDO-INSTRUCTION COUNTER must have been STEPPED by the
!       SUBJECT'S LENGTH.  "KV,$X2,I62PSI / SIC,SEN / BZXE,SERS" with
!       "-PSEUDO IC NOT STEPPED <n> CORRECTLY / -WHEN SUBJ INST WAS
!       <class>."
!
! RULE (c) IS THE WHOLE DIFFERENCE FROM TEST 1B.  TEST 1B
! (verify_ax5b_162_test1b_listing.py) sweeps the same five classes for
! plain EX with only (a) and (b).  Plain EX has no pseudo-instruction
! counter to step.  Reference Manual printed p.50 (PDF p.53; PDF page =
! printed page + 3), read at 400 dpi for this file:
!
!   EXECUTE (EX): "Bits 0-18 of the effective address form the address
!   of the location of a subject instruction that is fetched and
!   executed."
!
!   EXECUTE INDIRECT AND COUNT (EXIC): "Bits 0-18 of the full-word
!   addressed by bits 0-17 of the effective address are used as a
!   pseudo-instruction counter.  The contents of the pseudo-instruction
!   counter address the location of a subject instruction that is
!   fetched and executed.  After the subject instruction has been
!   fetched but prior to its execution, the pseudo-instruction counter
!   is stepped.  If the subject instruction is half-length, the
!   pseudo-instruction counter is stepped once; if full-length, twice."
!
! So the third rule exists BECAUSE EXIC has a pseudo-IC; it is not an
! extra check bolted onto the same shape.  And the deck makes the
! manual's "once / twice" executable: the four half-length classes check
! .32 (one half-word), and the FULL WD VFL class -- whose subject
! I62EXV is the full-word "L(BU),I00O" -- checks 1.0 (one full word):
!
!   023733.00  V+I,$X2,0.32   "-PSEUDO IC NOT STEPPED .32 CORRECTLY"
!   023772.40  V+I,$X2,1.0    "-PSEUDO IC NOT STEPPED 1.0 CORRECTLY"
!
! TWO IDIOMS FOR RULE (c), AND THE DECK USES BOTH.  DIR IX, the first
! class, checks the pseudo-IC ABSOLUTELY -- it never saves the "before"
! value, and instead builds the expected "after" value from the label:
!
!   023720.40  LVI,$X1,I62SUB+.32     24324.43 01
!   023721.00  KV,$X1,I62PSI          24323.02 90
!
! The other four check it RELATIVELY -- "LV,$X2,I62PSI" copies the
! pseudo-IC into $X2 BEFORE the EXIC, "V+I,$X2,<step>" adds the expected
! step AFTER it, and "KV,$X2,I62PSI" compares.  Both idioms are printed
! in this file's rows, which is why both are transcribed verbatim.
!
! THE HALF-WORD DIFFERENCE, RECORDED BECAUSE IT IS EASY TO "TIDY" AWAY.
! Each class's setup zeroes exactly the registers its subject writes:
! DIR IX and IMMED IX do "Z,$X1"; MISC does NOT (its subject IS "Z,$X1",
! so a nonzero value afterwards is the failure, and p.101 accordingly
! uses BZXVZ there); FLT PT does "Z,$L / Z,$R"; FULL WD VFL does "Z,$R"
! only.  Do not normalise.
!
! ------------------------------------------------------------------
! EVERY ERROR MESSAGE AND HEADING IN THIS FILE'S RANGE, VERBATIM
! ------------------------------------------------------------------
!   023705.00  "-TEST 2B, CHK EXIC OF NON BRANCH"
!   023705.40  "-CLASS INSTRUCTIONS, DIR IX."
!   023716.00  "-INT WHEN EXIC TO"
!   023716.40  "-A DIR IX INSTR."
!   023717.40  "-DIR IX WAS SUBJ INST."
!   023720.00  "-SUBJ INST OF EXIC NOT EXECUTED."
!   023721.40  "-PSEUDO IC NOT STEPPED .32 CORRECTLY"
!   023722.00  "-WHEN SUBJ INST WAS DIR IX."
!   023722.40  "-IMMED IX."
!   023730.40  "-INT WHEN EXIC TO"
!   023731.00  "-AN IMMED IX INST."
!   023732.00  "-SUBJ INST WAS IMMED IX,"
!   023732.40  "-AND WAS NOT EXECUTED."
!   023734.00  "-PSEUDO IC NOT STEPPED .32 CORRECTLY"
!   023734.40  "-WHEN SUBJ INST WAS IMMED IX."
!   023735.00  "-MISC"
!   023770.00  "-INT WHEN EXIC TO A"
!   023770.40  "-FULL WD VFL INSTR."
!   023771.40  "-SUBJ INST WAS FLT PT"
!   023772.00  "-AND WAS NOT EXECUTED."
!   023773.40  "-PSEUDO IC NOT STEPPED 1.0 CORRECTLY"
!   023774.00  "-WHEN SUBJ INST WAS VFL FULL WD."
!   023776.00  "-TO SSIP."
!   023777.00  "-UPDATE CONTINUITY CHECK."
!
! TYPO vs SCAN DAMAGE: NEITHER.  NOT ONE GARBLED GLYPH IN 76 ROWS.  Read
! at 600 dpi, every character above is a clean, well-inked print; no
! letter is ragged (damage) and none is a clean wrong letter in a word
! whose other instances are right (typo).  What the block DOES have is
! three CLEAN-PRINT DECK-AUTHORING inconsistencies, which are a
! different thing and are recorded, not corrected:
!
!   1. 023771.40 "-SUBJ INST WAS FLT PT" stands in the FULL WD VFL
!      class.  Its own pseudo-IC message two rows later was updated
!      ("-WHEN SUBJ INST WAS VFL FULL WD.") and this one was not.  The
!      clone-and-edit runs the other way on p.101, where the MISC and
!      FLT PT pseudo-IC messages still say "IMMED IX".
!   2. 023735.00 "-MISC" has NO trailing period, where every sibling
!      class heading has one ("-IMMED IX.", "-FLT PT.", "-FULL WD VFL.").
!      Checked on a tight 600 dpi crop of that one row: the C of MISC is
!      the last ink in the comment column, nothing follows it.  The
!      period on this chain is not a faint mark that could be lost -- it
!      segments as a ~29 px blob at 600 dpi.
!   3. 023732.00 "-SUBJ INST WAS IMMED IX," ends in a COMMA, where the
!      matching MISC and FLT PT rows on p.101 end in nothing and the DIR
!      IX row ends in a period.  Settled by the DESCENDER: the glyph
!      hangs below the baseline, and "-AN IMMED IX INST." one row above
!      ends in a period that does not.
!
! ------------------------------------------------------------------
! THE EXIT IS NOT THE SAME EXIT verify_ax5b_162_test3b_listing.py HAS
! ------------------------------------------------------------------
! 023774.40-024000.00 is the same five-row exit shape plus a continuity
! bridge, but THREE FIELDS DIFFER from the copy at 024162.40-024166.00:
!
!   here 023775.00  BD,I6260        there 024163.00  BD,I62100
!   here 023777.40  V+,$X13,BIT5    there 024165.40  V+,$X13,BIT8
!   here 023777.00  "-UPDATE CONTINUITY CHECK."
!                                   there 024165.00  "-UPDATE CONTINUITY."
!
! BIT5 vs BIT8 is the continuity mask bit for THIS test rather than for
! the routine; BD,I6260 is the restart link back to TEST 2B's own entry
! rather than to TEST 3A's.  Do not merge the two.
!
! ------------------------------------------------------------------
! ENCODING ONLY, and it could not be otherwise.  Rule (a) works by
! planting a handler address into the interrupt-table entry and awaiting
! an interruption, so a run needs the 64-word table, I60S1/I60SX1, and
! the I62EX* subject constants -- and EXIC is not EXECUTED by this model
! at all.  It is in MISC_CODES, so the ASSEMBLER encodes it; that is the
! whole distinction.
!
! Transcription standard: bit-exact against the printed machine code,
! verify_ax5b_162_test2b_head_tail_listing.py.

! ==================================================================
! HEAD -- PDF p.99 whole, plus its five-row spill onto PDF p.100.
! ==================================================================
        SLC, (8)23705.00
!
! ---- TEST 2B entry; DIR IX class: the setup ----------------------
I6260  LVI, $X1, I62INT          ! -TEST 2B, CHK EXIC OF NON BRANCH
        SV,  $X1, $IA             ! -CLASS INSTRUCTIONS, DIR IX.
        LVI, $X1, I6261           ! this class's rule-(a) error entry
        SVA, $X1, I62ITE          ! plant it in the interrupt-table entry
        LVI, $X1, I6262           ! this class's rule-(b) error entry
        SVA, $X1, I62BR1
        SVA, $X1, I62BR2
        LVI, $X1, I62SUB
        SVA, $X1, I62PSI          ! aim the pseudo-IC at the subject slot
        LX,  $X1, I62EX           ! the DIR IX subject instruction
        SX,  $X1, I62SUB
        SIC, I60SX1
        B,   I60S1                ! 1260's clear-indicators subroutine
        Z,   $IND
        Z,   $MASK
        Z,   $X1                  ! the subject will make it nonzero
        EXIC, I62PSI
        BD,  I6262                ! no interrupt: skip the rule-(a) entry
!
! ---- DIR IX class: rule (a) --------------------------------------
I6261  SIC, SEN                   ! -INT WHEN EXIC TO
        B,   SERS                  ! -A DIR IX INSTR.
!
! ---- DIR IX class: rules (b) and (c) -----------------------------
I6262  LX,  $X1, $X1
        SIC, SEN                   ! -DIR IX WAS SUBJ INST.
        BXVZ, SERS                 ! -SUBJ INST OF EXIC NOT EXECUTED.
        LVI, $X1, I62SUB+.32       ! the ABSOLUTE idiom: expected after
        KV,  $X1, I62PSI
        SIC, SEN                   ! -PSEUDO IC NOT STEPPED .32 CORRECTLY
        BZXE, SERS                 ! -WHEN SUBJ INST WAS DIR IX.
!
! ---- IMMED IX class: the setup -----------------------------------
        LVI, $X1, I6263           ! -IMMED IX.
        SVA, $X1, I62ITE
        LVI, $X1, I62SUB
        SVA, $X1, I62PSI
        LX,  $X1, I62EXI          ! the IMMED IX subject instruction
        SX,  $X1, I62SUB
        Z,   $IND
        Z,   $MASK
        Z,   $X1
        LV,  $X2, I62PSI          ! the RELATIVE idiom: pseudo-IC BEFORE
        EXIC, I62PSI
        BD,  I6264
!
! ---- IMMED IX class: rule (a) ------------------------------------
I6263  SIC, SEN                   ! -INT WHEN EXIC TO
        B,   SERS                  ! -AN IMMED IX INST.
!
! ---- IMMED IX class: rules (b) and (c) ---------------------------
I6264  LX,  $X1, $X1
        SIC, SEN                   ! -SUBJ INST WAS IMMED IX,
        BXVZ, SERS                 ! -AND WAS NOT EXECUTED.
        V+I, $X2, 0.32             ! one half-word: the subject is half-length
        KV,  $X2, I62PSI
        SIC, SEN                   ! -PSEUDO IC NOT STEPPED .32 CORRECTLY
        BZXE, SERS                 ! -WHEN SUBJ INST WAS IMMED IX.
!
! ---- MISC class: the setup; its error entries are on PDF p.101 ---
!   Note it does NOT do "Z,$X1": the MISC subject IS "Z,$X1", so a
!   nonzero index value afterwards is the failure, which is why p.101's
!   rule-(b) row is BZXVZ and not BXVZ.
        LVI, $X1, I6265           ! -MISC        (no trailing period, sic)
        SVA, $X1, I62ITE
        LVI, $X1, I62SUB
        SVA, $X1, I62PSI
        LX,  $X1, I62EXM          ! the MISC subject instruction
        SX,  $X1, I62SUB
! ---- PDF p.100 begins here; it prints these five rows and nothing else
        Z,   $IND
        Z,   $MASK
        LV,  $X2, I62PSI
        EXIC, I62PSI
        BD,  I6266

! ==================================================================
! TAIL -- PDF p.102.  The FULL WD VFL class's three error entries and
! routine 1262's TEST 2B exit.  023742.40-023767.40 in between is
! programs/ax5b_162_exic_classes.strap.
! ==================================================================
        SLC, (8)23770.00
!
! ---- FULL WD VFL class: rule (a) ---------------------------------
I6269  SIC, SEN                   ! -INT WHEN EXIC TO A
        B,   SERS                  ! -FULL WD VFL INSTR.
!
! ---- FULL WD VFL class: rules (b) and (c) ------------------------
!   The subject I62EXV is "L(BU),I00O", a FULL-LENGTH instruction, so
!   the pseudo-IC must step TWICE -- 1.0, not .32.  This row is the
!   whole reason p.101 alone cannot settle the stepping rule.
I6270  LX,  $X1, $R
        SIC, SEN                   ! -SUBJ INST WAS FLT PT   (stale, sic)
        BXVZ, SERS                 ! -AND WAS NOT EXECUTED.
        V+I, $X2, 1.0              ! one FULL WORD
        KV,  $X2, I62PSI
        SIC, SEN                   ! -PSEUDO IC NOT STEPPED 1.0 CORRECTLY
        BZXE, SERS                 ! -WHEN SUBJ INST WAS VFL FULL WD.
!
! ---- routine 1262's TEST 2B exit ---------------------------------
        B,   $+1.0                 ! computed target 023775.40; BIT 18 SET
        BD,  I6260                 ! the restart link: TEST 2B's own entry
        SIC, SEN0+.32
        B,   SSW                   ! -TO SSIP.
        BD,  $+.32
!
! ---- the continuity bridge ---------------------------------------
        LX,  $X13, IC262          ! -UPDATE CONTINUITY CHECK.
        V+,  $X13, BIT5           ! TEST 2B done = bit 5
        SX,  $X13, IC262
!
! ---- externals, SYN'd at the addresses this same deck prints -----
!   THESE ARE INPUTS TO THE CHECK, NOT WITNESSES.  No label row
!   defining any of them appears on PDF pp.99/100/102; every address
!   below comes from an OPERAND field or from another page.  See the
!   verify script's docstring for the tiering.
SEN     SYN, (8)1310.0             ! the SIC error-entry link
SERS    SYN, (8)1304.0             ! the error-report routine
SEN0    SYN, (8)1311.0             ! measured on PDF p.102: the DIGIT zero
SSW     SYN, (8)1301.0             ! -TO SSIP.
I60S1  SYN, (8)22741.0            ! 1260's clear-indicators subroutine
I60SX1 SYN, (8)23041.0            ! its SIC return link
I62INT SYN, (8)24220.0            ! the 64-word interrupt table
I62ITE SYN, (8)24320.0            ! the interrupt-table entry 1262 plants
I62EX  SYN, (8)24322.0            ! the DIR IX subject
I62PSI SYN, (8)24323.0            ! the pseudo-IC word
I62BR1 SYN, (8)24323.40           ! the RIGHT half of I62PSI's word
I62SUB SYN, (8)24324.0            ! the subject-instruction slot
I62BR2 SYN, (8)24325.0
I62EXM SYN, (8)24331.0            ! the MISC subject
I62EXI SYN, (8)24332.0            ! the IMMED IX subject
IC262  SYN, (8)24171.0            ! 1262's continuity register
BIT5   SYN, (8)24527.0            ! the BIT table's bit 5 word
I6265  SYN, (8)23742.40           ! MISC rule (a), PDF p.101
I6266  SYN, (8)23743.40           ! MISC rule (b), PDF p.101
        END, I6260
